  "note": "g06 was chosen as hero because it is the only fully daylit landscape shot and it conveys Liburnia's identity at a glance: the vine-covered terrace, antique stone mill, and produce cart together signal a rustic, generously furnished place before any copy is read. The gallery opens with that exterior, then moves into the warm evening dining room (g01) to show the indoor atmosphere, and closes with three food shots (g03, g04, g05) that progress from a single sizzling meat platter to a full table spread, giving a clear picture of the hearty cast-iron cooking. g02 was excluded from the gallery because its dark score of 3 and a figure dominating the frame make it unsuitable for site display.",
